# CLICKERMON

ClickerMon is a browser clicker game based on Pokemon that features Charmander, Charmeleon, and Charizard as useful upgrades to increase flow of coins.

# GITHUB REPOSITORY

https://github.com/yahirpre/CMPM121-D01Clicker

# LIVE APP

https://yahirpre.github.io/CMPM121-D01Clicker/

# IMPORTANT FILES

style.css -- Stylesheet
src/main.ts -- Where the game logic code exists
src/assets -- Asset files containing sprites used
index.html -- HTML file containing information regarding display organization and element IDs

# MEANINGFUL REVISIONS

HTML/CSS DISPLAY ORGANIZATION AND STYLE
structured the display to be centered with a more refined style compared to the default css options

REFACTORING
avoided repetitive or redundant code by implementing loops and functions where necessary
some important functions include...

    createTextElement() --  returns an HTMLElement containing text, including <p>, <h1>, <h2>,...
    createUpgradeButton() --  uses the upgrades object array to create buttons, descriptions, and event listeners based on those objects
    update()  --  updates the text with the newly calculated data. gets called after state changes such as coins incrementing or player clicks

DOM UPGRADE SYSTEM
used objects and object arrays to hold date regarding upgrades instead of repetitive code holding the same name, description, cost, costIncreaseFactor, and effect variables
